; Breakage 08: Well-typed OCaml that violates UDON Spec Ubiquitous Language invariants!
; - Asymmetric :dual (`reference` -> `referent`, but `referent` omits `:dual`)
; - `|avoid :word "node"` collides with defined term `node`!
; - Full-term `element` missing both invariants and examples!
; Expected: COMPILES cleanly with `ocamlc`, then caught by compiled `Checks.check_udon_spec`!

|document[broken-08]
  :context udon-spec

  |term[node].draft.foundation A vertex in an AST.
    :kind inline-term
    :pos  noun

  |term[element].draft.foundation An AST element (missing invariants and examples!).
    :kind full-term
    :pos  noun
    |avoid :word "node" \ collides with our own defined term «node»!

  |term[reference].draft Proxy for referents.
    :kind full-term
    :pos  noun
    :dual @[referent]
    |invariant Determination is deferred.

  |term[referent].draft Target of a reference (forgot back-link :dual @[reference]!).
    :kind full-term
    :pos  noun
    |invariant Exists independently of any reference.
